WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.230
<i>New Year's Eve.</i>

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.610
<i>Tonight, another year draws to a close.</i>

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.280
All right.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.330
Time to do some cleaning and ring in the new year right.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.500
Akira!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.080
Long time no talk, Ryo!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.590
Sorry! I gotta work during New Year's again.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.590
I think I'll be able to make it over
sometime over the holidays, though.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.050
I'm really sorry!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.680
Don't worry about it.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.520
Kirin's spending New Year's Eve here this year.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.140
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.310
Yep.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.310
Thanks for everything you've done this year, Akira.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.150
Here's to many more!

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.190
Right... Happy New Year.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.620
She didn't sound lonely at all.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.370
That just makes me feel lonelier.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.210
Screw it! I'm gonna get this done today if it kills me!

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.920
Not letting work keep me from my family anymore!

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.010
All right.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.680
Now that the big stuff's out of the way,

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.480
I can spend the rest of the day on the details.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.400
<i>Used toothbrushes and baking soda are great around the kitchen.</i>

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.400
<i>For screens, it's best to clean them with a sponge</i>

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:01.360
<i>and then dry them with newspaper to remove dirt and prevent water spots.</i>

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.910
<i>Mirrors sparkle spotlessly when polished with potato peel.</i>

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.000
And there we go. Nice and clean.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.340
The only thing left dirty...

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.340
is me.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.010
Don't you have more important things to do, Kirin?

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.270
Did you remember to book your ticket on the express?

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.400
It's fine. I'll just take the six o'clock.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.020
We can head down to the station later.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.690
Welcome!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:42.450
I don't think Kirin will be satisfied with just New Year's soba.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.910
What should I make for her?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.530
How about oden?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.750
I know it's a surprise to see each other here,
but I don't think it's anything to go weak-kneed over.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.750
Shiina... Your skin's so cold!

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.300
I saw you, so I thought I'd come up and say hi.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.470
It's not all that surprising.
And you didn't have to get that close.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.470
Thank you! Come again!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.310
I ended up buying a lot.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.100
Just having the ingredients for oden is exciting.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.310
You surprised me sneaking up like that,

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:20.610
but it's a really good idea to warm up with.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.700
It's also easy to make, and you can just keep picking at it.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.580
Why don't you come over too?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.330
The three of us can spend New Year's together.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.330
Sorry.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.420
I always spend New Year's at home. It's tradition.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.340
I wish the two of you could come over,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.800
but it's dangerous, so we don't let anyone else in.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.510
Anyway, see you.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.350
<i>What on Earth does Shiina's family do for New Year's?</i>

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.110
It smells great.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:01.980
Oh, right. I should tell Kirin.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.910
"I'm making oden tonight."

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.250
It really...

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.580
does smell great....

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.260
<i>She knows me too well.</i>

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.060
I-It's not like that!

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.810
I'm just making sure it's done!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.860
Oh, it's getting nice and soft.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.240
The unique aroma of dashi stock...

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.780
The alluring tint of light soy sauce...

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.790
The ingredients all simmering away happily together...

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.960
It's just too much!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.790
Fully-cooked oden is fine,

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:07.220
but this partially simmered, still slightly fresh oden has its own charm too.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:11.300
But I need to wait for Kirin...

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.890
Just a sample!

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.980
You need to sample to make sure!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:20.940
I'm making sure Kirin will have good oden!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.440
It's cooked through, at least.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.210
Starting with the luxurious centerpiece of the oden,

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:46.590
its gentle softness and earthy flavor seeping through my body...

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:58.680
Then a bit of konjac, which resists picking up other flavors even with slits carved in it...

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:02.770
When I taste it with a sip of the dashi-based broth,

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.150
it's like they're holding hands in my mouth!

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.150
Such springy happiness!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.410
I know I was only supposed to sample it,

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.910
but I can't help but reach out for more and more.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.160
My body is moving on its own!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.870
Kirin! Hurry up and get here!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.290
Kirin, we need to get going.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:29.300
Just a minute. My favorite comedian's about to—

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.430
Oh, by the way, I just got a call.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.930
Uncle Ryozo's on his way over.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:41.310
My dear Kirin, how you've grown!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.400
Th-Thank you...

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.690
Never mind! I'm ready to go!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.110
You really are afraid of grownups, aren't you?

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.660
Did you remember your ticket?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.490
Huh?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.330
I didn't bother booking a seat.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.330
I thought you said you were fine!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.540
It's New Year's! The train's going to be packed!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.040
You think so? The carriages are usually empty this far out.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.220
I should be fine without a reserved seat.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.430
The train is now departing.
Please wait for the next train.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.180
Looks like you'll have to wait for the next one.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.440
Wh-When's the next express?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.440
A whole hour?!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.980
You can't say I didn't warn you.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.700
I wish I hadn't watched TV for so long...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.740
I wish I'd booked a ticket!

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.410
If wishes were fishes, we'd all cast nets.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.620
Now hurry up and call Ryo.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.790
I'm so sorry!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.380
Oh, you missed your train?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:52.010
It's gonna be like two hours until I arrive.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.050
I wish I was there right now!

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.260
<i>Me too, Kirin.</i>

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.850
The oden and soba are wait—

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:03.600
You're supposed to be looking forward to seeing <i>her</i>.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.310
Don't worry about being late.

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:07.980
I don't want you too flustered when you get here.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.020
<i>Okay. But I'm still sorry.</i>

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.860
<i>Just relax with some TV and stay nice and toasty until I get there!</i>

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.570
Okay.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.620
Nice and toasty...

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:36.590
<i>I'm so excited to spend New Year's Eve with Kirin.</i>

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.510
I even came out to meet her.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.390
It's chilly!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.150
It's so warm holding hands!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.410
<i>This brings back memories.</i>

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.920
<i>It's been a year now.</i>

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.300
<i>I was so jealous of the people who had warm homes to go back to</i>

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.510
<i>and warm meals to share.</i>

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.510
<i>But now...</i>

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:28.850
<i>I have someone to share a warm meal with too.</i>

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.200
Ryo!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:39.610
Kirin?

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.780
You came to meet me?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.330
I'm so sorry I kept you waiting!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:47.960
There's still time until the year ticks over, so let's hurry!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:52.000
I want to hurry, too, but my legs are so cold they're like wood—

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:54.630
Ryo!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:58.760
Yikes! Your hands are so cold!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.140
I forgot my gloves.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.850
Hold on a sec.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.730
Kirin, your hands are so warm.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.140
They're soft, too. Like a baby's.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.360
Why a baby? Why can't they be soft like a mother's?!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.650
Sorry, sorry...

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.400
Are you warmed up now?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.870
Yep. Thanks.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:28.040
We've still got more than enough time, so let's take it easy.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.210
Yeah.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.880
You're like a little kid.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.300
A warm one, though.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.010
You smell good, Ryo.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.020
<i>The oden...</i>

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.730
You're making me blush.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.030
Ah. I feel alive again.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.030
Here you go. Warm soba and oden.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.910
I've been waiting for you!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:10.040
This is the warmest thing I've seen all year!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:16.000
There's plenty more where that came from, so dig in.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.800
Soba in a bowl?

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.940
The sweetness of the fluffy, crispy tempura shrimp

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:41.690
and the smooth soba noodles are warming me from the very bottom of my heart.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.830
The rainbow of flavors in the spices, broth, and simple soba noodles

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:57.710
blend so well that I can't focus on anything else!

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.710
Don't say that! We haven't even gotten to the oden!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.340
Oh, right.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:14.100
I love biting open the pouch of mochi that's soaked up all the flavor of the oden!

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.600
It's like getting a mouthful of all the other ingredients!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.860
I don't know if it's because I stopped the simmering and then started it again,

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.610
but the flavor of the stock has worked its way even deeper into the radish than before.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.120
Just pressing down on it with my teeth makes it all flow—

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.450
What do you mean, "before"?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.750
I can't eat another bite.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.590
I'll save the oden. We can have more later.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.090
Okay.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.720
Hey, they're ringing in the new year!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.430
This one's almost over, after all.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.470
It's exciting!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.060
Yep. There's something about the year changing that always makes my heart race.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.310
Ryo, you haven't finished your soba yet!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.770
Wait, aren't you supposed to eat it across the two years?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.690
No way!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.650
You've gotta finish it all in one year,

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:06.030
or you'll have bad luck!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.910
Really?!

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:08.780
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.280
Open wide!
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.530
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:18.080
Happy New Year!

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.460
Happy New Year!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.680
And the first thing we need to do in the new year is—

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.760
The dishes?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:34.560
What?!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.480
C'mon, it's New Year's!
We can do that later!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.850
I guess you're right.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.650
How about going to a shrine, then?

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.820
Going to a shrine right at the start of a new year? That's a great idea!

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.740
Grandma and I used to go as they rang the new year in.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:54.120
I think we'll be fine at the one in the neighborhood.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:58.000
Plus, we might be able to get
sweet sake from the neighbors.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.250
Th-The neighbors?!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.670
Oh, right. You have trouble with adults, right?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.090
No, I'll be okay!

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:09.260
I'm fine with Tsuyuko and Shiina's mom,

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.340
so I think this year I'm finally gonna get it under control!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.470
That's wonderful, Kirin!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.560
Plus, it'll only be for a little bit.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.600
If it gets too bad, I can just pretend I'm a cat!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.610
Do you mean "act catty"?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.150
Oh, Akira!

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.410
I did it...

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.910
I really did it!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.910
Oh, that's great! Happy New Year, Akira!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.880
I worked so hard to spend
New Year's Day with you, Ryo!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.340
I won't let work tear me away from my family anymore!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.840
Tear you away?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:52.090
Ah, your skin is as soft and springy as fresh mochi!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.800
Rub rub!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.930
Oh, Kirin!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.430
I... I haven't seen you in quite some time!

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.520
Allow me to wish you the most delightful of years!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.400
<i>She's gotten worse.</i>

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.900
Weren't you fine with Akira at the fair?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:14.820
I know, I know, but I think it's been so long that the new year just completely reset things.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.160
C'mon, what's wrong?

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.160
N-Nothing!

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.200
Well then, it's <i>your</i> turn for a rub!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.500
Rub ru—

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.580
Huh?

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.840
Kirin, do you have a little bit of
post-holidays stale mochi in you?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.670
H-Hey!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.170
See, that's more like you.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.610
To another good year!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:56.160
Look, they've got sweet sake!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.160
Here you go.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.420
Oh, hey, you're Machiko Akira!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.040
Yeah, that's me!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.590
It's been so long I barely recognized you!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.170
You've grown up quite the looker.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.550
Here, come and have a drink!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.510
Oh, thanks!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.680
Oh, Ryo, you came!

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:21.930
Yep.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.930
Happy New Year.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.480
And are you one of Ryo's friends?

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.400
Er... Yes!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.320
Thank you so much for everything you've done for my Ryo!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.990
"My" Ryo?!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:37.070
We have sweet sake. You two should have some too.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.990
S-Sweet sake?!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.700
Are we allowed to drink?

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:45.870
Sweet sake's made from the lees that remain after they make sake. It's non-alcoholic.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.460
Do you not you like sweet sake?

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.580
Oh, er...

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.670
It's my first time having any, so I'd be honored to!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.480
It's great!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.980
What is this? It's toasty warm and tastes like sweet rice!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.030
It's less a drink and more a dessert.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:22.490
And what's this complex sensation? It's fascinating!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.830
That's the sake lees.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:33.340
A soft sensation that's not quite solid and not quite liquid fills up your mouth...

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.920
It's warming me up from my tummy out!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.720
This is it! This is the taste of Japan!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.090
Thank you, god of rice!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.430
Your friend is so funny, Ryo.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.480
Especially the unique things she says.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.020
Unique?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:55.360
You're not doing that well at pretending to be a cat.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.030
The real you is shining through.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:02.870
I can't say I'm unhappy, but it's still a bit of a shock...

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.450
So, would you like more?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.120
Yeah, please!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.000
Fill me up!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.210
This is great!

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.130
Akira, you're no lightweight!

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.840
We're heading back, Akira.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.380
Oh, sure, go ahead.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:21.050
Stay safe! Follow the streetlights!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:21.090
All right, let's keep going until sunup!

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:25.010
Didn't Akira work extra hard so that she could spend New Year's with you?

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:29.560
It <i>is</i> New Year's, though.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.850
We're back!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.310
I guess we should finish off that oden.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.610
Really? After all that?

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.360
The walk kinda gave it all time to settle.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:45.370
Your appetite never ceases to amaze me, Kirin.

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:49.120
Come to think of it, isn't this what you cooked for me when we first met?

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.620
I think so, yeah.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.040
It's already been a whole year.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:56.630
That was the first time we ate together, wasn't it?

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:06.050
<i>Yep, that was when Kirin showed me just how wonderful food was when shared with someone else.</i>

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.060
This is great!

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.350
It's just as good as back then.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:13.940
Huh?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:17.190
Your cooking's always so warm and caring. I love it!

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.700
Thank you very much.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.780
But I couldn't do it all on my own.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:31.040
It's because you're here eating with me that it tastes so good.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.330
Even if the preparation and the seasoning are the same,

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.420
it's so, so much tastier this way than eating alone.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:44.720
Wait, am I made of spice or something?

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.550
I don't <i>think</i> I taste good...

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.810
I didn't mean it like that.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.060
Or are you trying to hide a blush?

00:20:55.190 --> 00:21:00.070
The year we've known each other has gone by in a flash.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.570
At this rate, maybe we'll be all grown up before we know it.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.990
But first, we've got to get into high school.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.830
Oh, right.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.460
<i>I hope that even after we grow up,</i>

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:20.590
<i>I'll be able to sit together with Kirin like this.</i>

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:25.470
I hope we can still eat together, even after we've grown up.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:28.550
Me too!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:38.060
Akira's been out like a light ever since she came back this morning, huh?

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:41.440
She worked hard all year.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.690
Let's let her get some rest.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.740
Anyway, see you next week!

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.490
Or should I say, see you this year?

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.500
"See you this year" sounds kind of funny.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.750
Oh well.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.300
See you this year!

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:45.020
Those two get along so well.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:48.230
They're like cheese and tomatoes.

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:56.740
The soft, tender cheese wraps around sprightly, sun-ripened tomato.

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.200
And what does that make me, you ask?

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:02.000
I guess I'd be... the basil!

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.040
Tee-hee!

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:06.590
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:09.050
Crispy and Chewy!
